General structure:

ALTER TABLE table_name
    operation1,
    operation2,
    operation3;

1. Columns
Operation	Syntax
Add column	ADD COLUMN
Modify column	MODIFY COLUMN
Rename column	RENAME COLUMN
Rename + modify column	CHANGE COLUMN
Remove column	DROP COLUMN

Add

ALTER TABLE students
ADD COLUMN age INT;

Add multiple

ALTER TABLE students
ADD COLUMN age INT,
ADD COLUMN email VARCHAR(100),
ADD COLUMN city VARCHAR(50);

Modify datatype/properties

ALTER TABLE students
MODIFY COLUMN age BIGINT NOT NULL;

Rename

ALTER TABLE students
RENAME COLUMN name TO full_name;

Rename + modify

ALTER TABLE students
CHANGE COLUMN name full_name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL;

Remove

ALTER TABLE students
DROP COLUMN age;

2. PRIMARY KEY
Add
ALTER TABLE students
ADD PRIMARY KEY (student_id);

Remove
ALTER TABLE students
DROP PRIMARY KEY;

You can also use multiple columns:

ALTER TABLE students
ADD PRIMARY KEY (student_id, course_id);

This is called a composite primary key.

3. UNIQUE constraint
Add
You don't have to provide a constraint name:

ALTER TABLE students
ADD UNIQUE (email);

Or give it a name:

ALTER TABLE students
ADD CONSTRAINT uq_email UNIQUE (email);

Remove
ALTER TABLE students
DROP INDEX email;

If you gave it a constraint/index name:

ALTER TABLE students
DROP INDEX uq_email;

4. FOREIGN KEY
Add
ALTER TABLE students
ADD FOREIGN KEY (department_id)
REFERENCES departments(id);

Or with a name:

ALTER TABLE students
ADD CONSTRAINT fk_department
FOREIGN KEY (department_id)
REFERENCES departments(id);

Remove
If the foreign key is named fk_department:

ALTER TABLE students
DROP FOREIGN KEY fk_department;

5. CHECK constraint
Add
ALTER TABLE students
ADD CHECK (age >= 18);

Or name it:

ALTER TABLE students
ADD CONSTRAINT chk_age CHECK (age >= 18);

Remove
If named:

ALTER TABLE students
DROP CHECK chk_age;

6. NOT NULL
NOT NULL is a column attribute, so you modify the column.

Add NOT NULL
ALTER TABLE students
MODIFY COLUMN name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL;

Remove NOT NULL
ALTER TABLE students
MODIFY COLUMN name VARCHAR(100) NULL;

7. DEFAULT value
Add/change DEFAULT
ALTER TABLE students
ALTER COLUMN status SET DEFAULT 'active';

Remove DEFAULT
ALTER TABLE students
ALTER COLUMN status DROP DEFAULT;

You can also use MODIFY:

ALTER TABLE students
MODIFY COLUMN status VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'active';

8. AUTO_INCREMENT
Add AUTO_INCREMENT
For example:

