    WHEN marks >= 80 THEN 'A'
    WHEN marks >= 60 THEN 'B'
    ELSE 'Fail'
END

If marks are 30:

30 >= 80 → false
30 >= 60 → false

Therefore:

ELSE → Fail

ELSE is optional.

You can technically write:

