    WHEN marks >= 80 THEN 'A'
    WHEN marks >= 60 THEN 'B'
END

If none of the conditions match, MySQL returns NULL.

Generally, using ELSE is safer and clearer.

END
END tells MySQL:

"The CASE expression is finished."

CASE
